{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["כאשר ירים משה — his hand and the staff." "וגבר ישראל — for thus is the way of arrayers of battle: as long as they see the raising of standards, קונפט\"ן in Old French, they prevail, and when it is cast down they are accustomed to flee and be defeated."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {1 "The Old French gloss קונפט\"ן (conp[te]n or similar) is left untranslated; its precise form and meaning are uncertain. The letter bet in ב\"ל may stand for 'bellesh' or 'bel'='Old French' (vieil), but the abbreviation is not fully resolved."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:41:51.556039340Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}